<title>GERMANY: Allianz names new board member for German unit.</title>
<headline>Allianz names new board member for German unit.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A former Citibank AG board member is join the management board of Germany's Allianz AG Holding's domestic non-life unit, Allianz said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Joachim Faber, 46, will join the Allianz Versicherungs AG board on April 1 where he will take over responsibility for asset management, Allianz said in a statement.</p>
<p>Alexander Hoyos, the former head of asset management on the Allianz Versicherungs AG management board, is to take responsibility for Allianz's Austrian units.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
